## RP-1 spec sabotage → `openspec validate 2026-10-30-seat-heal`
Baseline sha256 of openspec/changes/2026-10-30-seat-heal/specs/seat-heal/spec.md:
  e4f87844a496e8a2d5aec8133963d05ff6c32b5bbe79f7bcc66325abc6a2d37f (84 lines)
- Probe A (rename one Scenario title): validate rc=0 GREEN. Scenario titles are not schema-guarded.
- Probe B (remove ONE full Scenario block, requirement keeps 1 scenario): validate rc=0 GREEN.
  Finding (informational, NOT a wave defect): `openspec validate` guards "each requirement has
  >=1 Scenario", not scenario count. Single-scenario removal is caught by reviewer/drift-guard
  diff review, not by validate. The check is therefore narrow but NOT vacuous (see Probe C).
- Probe C (RED): removed BOTH REQ-SH1 scenarios (lines 28-39, requirement left with zero scenarios).
  Command: `openspec validate 2026-10-30-seat-heal` → exit rc=1 RED.
  Error: `✗ [ERROR] seat-heal/spec.md: ADDED "REQ-SH1 — kickoff re-verification with scope cap" must include at least one scenario`
- Restore: `git checkout -- <spec.md>` → sha256 e4f87844… (byte-identical) →
  `openspec validate` rc=0 GREEN ("Change '2026-10-30-seat-heal' is valid"). `git status --short` clean.
- Extra (same session): garbage spec (no delta sections) → validate --strict rc=1 RED
  ("Change must have at least one delta... each requirement MUST include at least one #### Scenario: block");
  restored byte-identical. `openspec validate nonexistent-change-xyz` prints "Unknown item" but exits 0
  (upstream CLI behavior — item-name typos are NOT fail-closed; noted for coordinator awareness).

